  "creditFinding": "60 common year 1, 60 PPP year 2 and 60 year 3. Year 3 contains 10 exploration, 15 thesis, 5 professional impact, 30 open electives. The free-elective catalogue entry is informational and does not add credits to its enclosing group.",
  "progression": {
    "y2-fieldwork": "Pass the required first-year writing, research, ethics and statistics courses. Pass both research design contributions before starting the three-week January fieldwork. Tutorials, lectures and the closing conference are compulsory.",
    "y2-research-preparation": "The first-year research, ethics, writing and statistics requirements also apply to this preparation course.",
    "y2-multivariate": "Finish the Fieldwork NL research period and pass the required first-year courses before starting multivariate analysis.",
    "y3-religion": "One of the two 10-EC exploration options in this specialisation. Entry requires completion of the first year, Research Preparation, Fieldwork NL and both specialisation Key Issues courses.",
    "y3-thesis": "The 15-EC project combines thematic preparation, a proposal and an individual thesis. Entry requires the completed first year, Diversity and Power and at least one Key Issues course specific to the specialisation.",
    "y3-impact": "Complete the first- and second-year Academic Skills and Research Lab courses and Diversity and Power before registering.",
    "y3-electives": "The 30 EC may be used for approved electives, a minor, exchange or eligible internship arrangements. The allocation does not prescribe a particular package."
  },
  "zeroCredit": [
    "6491TUT19Y first-year tutoring required for positive BSA",
    "6492TUTY and 6493TUTY career orientation"
  ],
  "scope": "2026–2027 official route/module records. The 2025–2026 regulations are historical leads. The formal 2026–2027 rules did not need to be substituted for the coherent current catalogue.",
  "timing": "Culture and Comparison in block 1 precedes Culture and Globalisation in block 2. The Fieldwork NL catalogue schedule places the three-week research period in January, before Multivariate Analysis in block 3. Fieldwork tutorials and final conference continue later in the year. The requirement is to finish the research period before starting statistics. Both design contributions must pass before fieldwork begins. The ordinary pathway completes first- and second-year requirements before all third-year courses.",
